Consider the following C code. How would ASan detect a buffer overflow if compiled and run with `-fsanitize=address`?
```c
#include <string.h>
#include <stdlib.h>
int main() {
    char *buf = (char*)malloc(10);
    strcpy(buf, "This string is too long for the buffer.");
    free(buf);
    return 0;
}
```
